# Git branch policy

**Never create a new git branch unless the user explicitly asks you to.**

- Default workflow: commit and push on the branch the user is already on (usually `main` or `master`).
- Do not run `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, or equivalent proactively — not for PRs, not for "best practice", not to isolate work.
- If a PR is needed on the current branch, use `gh pr create` from that branch after push.
- Only create a feature branch when the user clearly says to (e.g. "create a branch", "new branch for this", "branch off main").

When unsure which branch to use, ask — do not branch on your own.
